      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Hand, Foot, Mouth Disease (HFMD) is a highly contagious enteroviral infection with the potential for significant morbidity. In recent years, there has been an increase in atypical cutaneous manifestations of HFMD. We present a pilot case series utilizing Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) testing of lesional skin to render a diagnosis of HFMD. These preliminary results suggest that lesional skin PCR testing could be an effective and minimally-invasive test for diagnosing HFMD. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved."
      },
